<section image-layout="blank" id="3qt0QpLHtM"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="1opVfQguwm" background-color="accent" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">THE INVISIBLE SHIELD CLUB · MISSION 01</p><display size="md">Follow one UV ray</display><h3 role="subheading">Find Earth’s invisible ozone shield.</h3><p font-size="lg">High above the weather, ozone absorbs much of the Sun’s harmful ultraviolet radiation. Today you will spot ozone, predict what changes and explain how people protect it.</p><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item background-color="palette-3" padding="12pt 16pt"><p font-size="18pt"><b>MISSION</b> Spot O₃ → predict UV → protect together.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item background-color="surface" padding="8pt 12pt"><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP ozone assessment</a></p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="7v4WM39aqT" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/H0HMR0HoI1NmcAWHrHsyc.png" saved-media-id="r6l8a8p1w4xlhdg" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="atmosphere-cut-paper" alt="Layered cut-paper editorial science illustration of Earth curving across the lower right, cloud-white land beneath a thin shield-blue atmospheric arc, several UV-gold sunlight paths arriving from the upper left with some ending in the blue region and some continuing, deep-ink outer space, clean vector-like edges, subtle paper fibers, bright optimistic mood, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>